<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 243)</h2>
<p><b>No comment lost to permissions.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>In a shared review, whoever publishes carries <b>everyone's</b> notes — each line keeps its author's name, so an unassigned reviewer's comment reaches the Kitsu task under their own name via the publisher.</li>
<li>If your own publish is refused because Kitsu says you're not assigned to the task, the <b>studio bot posts it for you</b> — your name bolded on the comment — and the panel tells you that's what happened. (Only on machines that hold the bot token; guest seats never do.)</li>
<li>Project team members already see every task in the project; if your review team should also comment directly as themselves anywhere, give them Kitsu's <b>supervisor</b> role — the manual explains the mapping.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
